{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multi agent specialization threshold multi agent specialization threshold","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md","fileName":"Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Multi-Agent Incident Response]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Multi-Agent Incident Response","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multi agent specialization threshold multi agent specialization threshold","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md","fileName":"Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold","heading":"Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Multiple agents are justified when a task contains distinct expertise domains, independent checks, or evidence-gathering work that benefits from parallel execution. Incident response can meet this threshold because deployment history, runtime health, runbook compliance, remediation, and communication are separable responsibilities.\n\nA single agent remains preferable when one bounded context and tool set can solve the task. Adding agents creates coordination, validation, latency, and failure-handling costs. Specialization should therefore improve evidence quality or reduce context and tool overload, not merely make the architecture appear advanced.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Multi-Agent Incident Response","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multi agent specialization threshold multi agent specialization threshold","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md","fileName":"Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multi-Agent Specialization Threshold","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Multi-Agent Incident Response","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}